\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The fields are all white,
\par And the reapears are few;
\par We children are willing,
\par But what can we do
\par To work for the Lord in His harvest?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Our hands are so small,
\par And our words are so weak:
\par We cannot teach others;
\par How then shall we seek
\par To work for our Lord in His harvest?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. We'll work by our prayers,
\par By the offerings we bring,
\par By small self-denials;
\par The least little thing
\par May work for our Lord in His harvest:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Until by and by,
\par As the years pass, at length
\par We too may be reapers,
\par And go forth in strength,
\par To work for our Lord in His harvest.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

